      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "c9a86f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "This agreement displays all lower-division courses required in the major: CSU Northridge courses on the left, approved (articulated) transfer courses to the right. General education (Cal-GETC or CSU Northridge GE) and upper-division courses are also required to complete the bachelor's degree. Completion of all coursework listed in this agreement is not mandatory prior to admission. For CSU Northridge Undergraduate Admission Requirements , refer to Upper Division Transfer . Some coursework may be satisfied by Advanced Placement exams completed in high school. Visit AP Credit for information. Additional information about the major is available in the CSUN University Catalog . Questions regarding this agreement may be directed to: articulation@csun.edu .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong>This agreement displays all lower-division courses required in the major:</strong> CSU Northridge courses on the left, approved (articulated) transfer courses to the right. General education (Cal-GETC or CSU Northridge GE) and upper-division courses are also required to complete the bachelor's degree.</p><p><br></p><p>Completion of all coursework listed in this agreement is not mandatory prior to admission. For CSU Northridge Undergraduate <strong>Admission Requirements</strong>, refer to <a href=\"http://www.csun.edu/admissions-records/apply-upper-division-transfer-student#eligible\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Upper Division Transfer</a>.</p><p><br></p><p>Some coursework may be satisfied by Advanced Placement exams completed in high school. Visit <a href=\"http://catalog.csun.edu/policies/advanced-placement-ap-credit/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">AP Credit</a> for information. Additional information about the major is available in the <a href=\"http://catalog.csun.edu/programs/major/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">CSUN University Catalog</a>.</p><p><br></p><p>Questions regarding this agreement may be directed to: <a href=\"mailto:articulation@csun.edu\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">articulation@csun.edu</a>.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "cba26f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "INTERDISCIPLINARY STUDIES Methodological Course Requirements",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "c0a26f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "Students will choose two courses from the Cultural Approaches to Interdisciplinarity requirement and one course from each of the following three requirements: Logic, Literacy and Rhetoric; Quantitative Approaches to Complex Problems; Qualitative Approaches to Complex Problems The courses listed below are applicable in the following requirements: Quantitative Approaches to Complex Problems Basic Business Statistics Lower Division Cultural Approaches to Interdisciplinarity Introduction to Asian American Studies Gender, Sexuality, and American Indian Communities Introduction to Central American Studies Race, Racism, and Critical Thinking Gateways to Western Civilization: Greece and Rome Jewish Religion and Culture Language(s) in California American Religious History and Ideals",
      "contentHtml": "<p>Students will choose two courses from the Cultural Approaches to Interdisciplinarity requirement and one course from each of the following three requirements: Logic, Literacy and Rhetoric; Quantitative Approaches to Complex Problems; Qualitative Approaches to Complex Problems</p><p><br></p><p>The courses listed below are applicable in the following requirements:</p><p><br></p><p><u>Quantitative Approaches to Complex Problems</u></p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Basic Business Statistics</em></li></ul><p><br></p><p><u>Lower Division Cultural Approaches to Interdisciplinarity</u></p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Introduction to Asian American Studies</em></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Gender, Sexuality, and American Indian Communities</em></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Introduction to Central American Studies</em></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Race, Racism, and Critical Thinking</em></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Gateways to Western Civilization: Greece and Rome</em></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Jewish Religion and Culture</em></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Language(s) in California</em></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>American Religious History and Ideals</em></li></ul>"
    }
  ],
